            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0669" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 21558/5.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Straus to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-10-09"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">October 9, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Straus says that the Porte claims that as Rizk is a Turkish subject, it can
                    not consent to his extradition and can not ask the Egyptian <pb facs="0670"
                        n="598" xml:id="pg598"/> authorities to extradite him. Says Porte has
                    neither admitted nor strenuously denied validity of treaty of 1874, but admits
                    if it is valid in Turkey it is valid in Egypt. Mr. Straus says he will press the
                    matter further. Adds that according to Ottoman law, a Turkish subject who has
                    committed a crime in a foreign country against another Turkish subject and has
                    not been tried in the foreign country can be tried in Turkey. Says he does not
                    know the Egyptian law on this point.</p>
            </div>
